[=#postgresqlpasswords]
= Password Method =

By default, the !PostgreSQL protocol module challenges a connecting client for an md5 hash of its password rather than the password itself.  Setting the //passwords// attribute on the listener tag to "cleartext" makes the module accept the password itself instead.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-postgresqlfecleartext.conf@
}}}
}}}

Cleartext passwords are required when a one-way password encryption module is used for a database user's password - see [secpwdenc.html Password Encryption] for why - and sends the password over the network as typed, so it should only be used with TLS or on a trusted network.

----

